    97	
    98	Per family, base and doubled: runner-up minus R3, C* minus runner-up, and C* minus R3, each against the rule's unchanged
    99	frozen reference (doubled: the runner-up's doubling records and the report's held-out records for R3 and C*), from
   100	unrounded per-seed values. Per market and pooled estimates, each with a nominal paired percentile bootstrap interval
   101	(9,999 resamples, seed 0, seeds resampled within each market, the same indices for both rules). The registered Q1
   102	categories are applied to the nominal pooled interval with the margin 0.05, labelled exploratory. The intervals are
   103	conditional on these six markets and the selected policies and references; they exclude search and market-sampling
   104	uncertainty and carry no registered calibration or Holm guarantee. The doubling check's attack and reference changes
   105	and its flag are reported per cell.
   106	
   107	## 4. Expectation (written before any runner-up result)
   108	
   109	E: pooled g(C*) - g(C-thr12) > 0 under D2+H3, computed exactly from the paired per-seed values (not against a rounded
   110	threshold). Met if it holds under both base and doubled records; failed if it fails under both (a tie, exactly 0, is not
   111	met); not established if they disagree; "not available" if a record is missing or a value is nonfinite (reported
