   119	(x 1.25 = 2.49); **stop cap and reservation 3.00 USD**, the full allowance, in the ledger category `followup` (cap 22 USD
   120	shared by all follow-up runs: reset 5, churn 8, Run A 3, Run B 4.25, total 20.25; `budget_followup.py reserve`). A paid run
   121	requires `--started-at <allocation time>` and the launcher's attempts file (`--attempts`). The driver checks
   122	the cap between stages: a stage starts only if the billed time so far
   123	plus its estimate stays within the cap; a running stage is never killed (author's instruction); the run stops, writes
   124	`cost_stop.json` and an inventory, and reports. This is an admission limit, not a billing ceiling: a stage that starts
   125	within the cap finishes, and the pod is deleted after it.
   126	
   127	**Launcher handoff (draft 5).** The launcher copy pushes to the pod, before every paid driver call, its current
   128	`<name>.attempts` file and the ledger, and passes `--attempts`, `--ledger`, `--run-tag`, `--started-at` (the current pod's
   129	allocation time), `--usd-per-hour` (the price ceiling MAXCPH), `--stop-file /root/STOP`, and `--soft-deadline` (its soft
   130	deadline). The driver reads the launcher's own event lines (`<pod> <epoch> start`, `<pod> <epoch> deleted`;
   131	`guards.attempts_spend`): each closed attempt counts at the ceiling, the open start is the current pod (counted from
   132	`--started-at`), and malformed or unordered lines are refused (tests with lines in the launcher's exact format); spend of
   133	earlier launches comes from the ledger rows tagged with the run tag, since the launcher truncates its file per launch. The
   134	driver checks the STOP file and the soft deadline before each internal stage or round, so a single `--stage all` call
   135	honours the launcher's between-stage stop (test).
   136	
   137	**Admission before every paid step (draft 6).** Before the pod's first paid step, and before each later one (the reset
   138	reproduction gate included), the launcher runs `python3 docs/revision/followup2/guards.py admit --cap-usd 3.00
   139	--usd-per-hour <ceiling> --started-at <allocation> --attempts <file> --ledger <ledger> --run-tag runner-up --hours <step estimate>
   140	--stop-file /root/STOP --soft-deadline <soft>` and starts the step only on exit 0. Reservation: `budget_followup.py
